  "Body": {
    "ContentType": "html",
    "Content": "<p>Update Management has added a new option for update deployments. When you edit or create a new update deployment, there&#39;s a field called <strong>Reboot options</strong>. You can use these&nbsp;to control if and when a machine will reboot.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>To learn more about this new capability, visit the <a href=\"https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/automation/automation-tutorial-update-management#schedule-an-update-deployment\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">documentation page</a>.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><img alt=\"New update deployment screen showing reboot options\" src=\"https://azurecomcdn.azureedge.net/mediahandler/acomblog/updates/ServiceUpdates/blog/b9d6b0e8-cd0b-4387-8683-4806c84059a9.png\" title=\"New Update Deployment - Reboot Options\"></p>\r\n",
    "Markdown": "Update Management has added a new option for update deployments. When you edit or create a new update deployment, there's a field called Reboot options . You can use these to control if and when a machine will reboot.\n\nTo learn more about this new capability, visit the documentation page ."
  },
